<HELPSTRUCTURE>\
 <HELPCATEGORY CAPTION="About VMK">
  <HELP NAME="help.introduction.what" CAPTION="What Is VMK?">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Disney's Virtual Magic Kingdom is a free online multiplayer game that lets you experience the awesome magic of Disney Theme Parks from home.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Live inside of Disney's virtual world to create your own experiences, control your online Character and interact with Players from around the globe!]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[And it doesn't stop there. Visit a Disney Theme Park for your chance to win cool gear, magic spells and fun surprises to enhance your VMK gameplay. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Play in-park Quests at Disneyland® park at Disneyland® Resort or the Magic Kingdom Park® at Walt Disney World® Resort to help you rule the virtual Kingdom!]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.about.safety" CAPTION="Help & Safety">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[We encourage you to do a few simple things to keep safe from any uncomfortable situations:\r
* Always keep a parent or guardian informed that you are playing VMK.\r
* Have fun and follow the VMK Values.
]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[* Be aware that there are players who may attempt to cheat you out of your credits and stuff.\r
* Always feel free to CALL FOR HELP if you're being bothered by another player.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Do remember that you are in control. If another player is making you uncomfortable, you can IGNORE them, BOOT them from your guest room, or REPORT them to VMK Staff. And if things get out of hand, you can always EXIT the game and come back later.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[IGNORE A PLAYER\r
Simply click on their character to open their profile. (Their profile is the window with their signature and pins.) Click the red IGNORE button and you won't have to see what they type for a while.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[BOOT A PLAYER\r
If someone's causing trouble in your guest room you can boot them out. Open their profile, then click the red BOOT button. The troublesome player will be thrown out of your room and won't be allowed to return for 15 minutes.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[DELETE FRIEND\r
If you want to remove someone from your friend list, select their name and click the red DELETE button. This will stop them from sending you messages, and they won't be able to see your location in the game anymore.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[CALL FOR HELP\r
To get emergency help at any time while you're playing the game, simply CALL FOR HELP by clicking the other tab in this window. A VMK staff member will then either send you a message or come and see you.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Talk to an adult you know well if you're worried or upset about anything that's happened online. If there is no adult you can speak to, or if you want to talk to someone in confidence, you can call Childhelp USA at 1-800-4-A-CHILD (1-800-422-4453).]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.about.cm" CAPTION="VMK Staff">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[VMK staff members are carefully selected and fully-trained moderators. They can send warnings to misbehaving players, kick them out of rooms or even ban them from the game.
 



]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can identify VMK Staff by clicking on their character in the game and checking for a badge in their profile. A VMK Staff badge is orange and has a Mickey Mouse picture on it. When you click on the badge, you'll see that its name is 'VMK Staff'.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[To get emergency help at any time while you're playing the game, simply CALL FOR HELP by clicking the other tab in this window. A VMK staff member will then either send you a message or come and see you.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If someone is sending you offensive messages in the game, you can report them to VMK Staff by clicking the red REPORT button. You can also report a player simply by clicking on their character and choosing the red REPORT button in their profile.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[The CALL FOR HELP option is VMK's 911 service, so please only use it in emergencies — if another player is hassling you or making you feel uncomfortable. For general questions about the game, see the game guide.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[And do remember that you are in control. If another player is making you uncomfortable, you can IGNORE them, BOOT them from your guest room, or REPORT them to VMK Staff. And if things get out of hand, you can always EXIT the game and come back later.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If you have any questions, or issues with VMK Staff, please use the CONTACT US form on the website: www.vmk.com]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Talk to an adult you know well if you're worried or upset about anything that's happened online. If there is no adult you can speak to, or if you want to talk to someone in confidence, you can call Childhelp USA at 1-800-4-A-CHILD (1-800-422-4453).]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.about.cl" CAPTION="Community Leaders">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Community Leaders are experienced and enthusiastic players who help out in VMK. A Community Leader can answer some of your questions about the game and may sometimes organize fun events. For help with a serious matter, contact VMK staff members.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can identify a Community Leader by clicking on their character and checking for a badge in their profile. A Community Leader badge is blue and has a Sorcerer Mickey hat on it. When you click on the badge, you'll see that its name is 'Community Leader.']]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If you've been playing VMK for a while and you have a clean record (no bans!), maybe you could become our next Community Leader. Read up on the VMK Values first, then apply via the CONTACT US form on the website: www.vmk.com]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If you want to send us feedback on any of our Community Leaders, please use the CONTACT US form on the website: www.vmk.com]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.about.values" CAPTION="VMK Values">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Virtual Magic Kingdom is a free multi-player game, where you can have a Disney Theme Park experience and hang out with your friends. Many VMK players are between the ages of 10-14, so VMK needs to be a safe, non-threatening environment.
]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[The rules are very simple. Stick to them and everyone will have fun; break them and you'll get yourself banned from the game.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[YOU SHOULD:\r
* Have fun!\r
* Hang out with your friends.\r
* Chat with new people.\r
* Respect other people's views and beliefs.
]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[YOU MUST NOT:\r
* Use ANY hacking, scripting or editing program with the game.\r
* Steal other players' credits or in-game belongings.\r
* Describe sexual acts to other Players.\r
* Pester people who don't want to talk to you.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[YOU MUST NOT:\r
* Swear or use sexually graphic or racist terms.\r
* Ask other players for their passwords, email addresses, IM, telephone numbers or other personal information.\r
* Give away, trade or sell your VMK character.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[YOU MUST NOT:\r
* Type your password anywhere except in the Disney registration and log-in pages, or in the Contact Us section of the website. \r
* Break the law in the game or talk others into breaking it.
]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[For more information to make gameplay as safe as possible, please read the Safety Section of the website: www.vmk.com]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
 </HELPCATEGORY>
 <HELPCATEGORY CAPTION="Your Character">
  <HELP NAME="help.character.name" CAPTION="Your VMK Guest Name">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[The VMK staff members will read your name to make sure it's appropriate for the Virtual Kingdom. Until they've approved it, you will have a temporary name, e.g. 'Guest1234'. If they can't approve your name, you will get the chance to think of a new one.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.character.sig" CAPTION="Updating Your Signature">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can change your signature at any time to reflect your mood or what you're up to in the game. Your signature is a one-liner that other Guests see when they click on your Character in the game.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[To update your sig, open the 'Preferences' menu by clicking the t-shirt icon at the bottom of the game screen.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[To keep VMK safe and welcoming, your signature can only contain words that are in VMK's allowed words list. Words that aren't recognized as suitable flash in red, and you'll have to change them before you can save your sig.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If you're having trouble saying what you want to (for example, if your favorite new song includes some words that aren't in our dictionary), you can suggest a new word to us via the Contact Us form on the website.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.character.pins" CAPTION="Wearing Pins">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Collect and wear Disney pins! To collect pins, visit the shop in each land to see what it has on offer. You can buy designer pins with your in-game credits.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[And you'll be rewarded with exclusive pins for finding Disney Characters (like The Yeti and Shrunken Ned), winning the multiplayer games, or finding Hidden Mickeys.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can manage your Pins by viewing your 'Stuff' – click the chair icon at the bottom of the screen and then select the Pins tab. Simply choose a pin and click 'Wear' to show it in your profile. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[The pins that are already in your profile are listed in the 'Pins Worn' section. Select one of these pins and click 'Take Off' to remove it from your profile. You can wear a maximum of 8 pins at a time.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.characters.badges" CAPTION="Badges">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[There are 5 different badges in VMK: \r
* VMK Staff\r
* Community Leader\r
* Born in Park\r
* VIP\r
* Here From Day 1\r
Badges display in your profile but don't show up in your inventory, because they can't be traded.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[VMK Staff:\r
VMK staff members are carefully selected and fully-trained moderators. A VMK Staff badge is orange and has a Mickey Mouse picture on it. When you click on the badge, you'll see that its name is 'VMK Staff'.
    
]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Community Leader:\r
Community Leaders are experienced and enthusiastic Players who help out in the Kingdom. The CL badge is blue and has a Sorcerer Mickey hat pictured on it. When you click on the badge, you'll see that its name is 'Community Leader'.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Born in Park:\r
Any VMK Characters created inside Disneyland® park or the Magic Kingdom Park® have an exclusive 'Born in Park' badge. This badge is green and has a VMK-styled Castle.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[VIP:\r
Any VMK players who complete an in-park Quest at Disneyland® or Walt Disney World® are rewarded with a VIP badge to help them rule the virtual Kingdom!]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Here From Day 1:\r
This exclusive gold badge was given to all of the players who joined VMK during our 'beta' period.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
 </HELPCATEGORY>
 <HELPCATEGORY CAPTION="Moving Around">
  <HELP NAME="help.navigation.walking" CAPTION="Walking Around">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[It's easy to move inside a room: just click the ground where you want your Character to walk. If your feet need a rest, click on or under chairs and benches to sit down.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[And if you want to shake your stuff, or wave to a friend, open the emote menu by the chat bar (it's the heart-shaped icon), and select 'Dance' or 'Wave.']]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If you want to explore further, simply exit the room and see where you end up. You can walk from one end of the Kingdom to the other! You'll find exits at the edges of the room - they're marked with a red cursor.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If you want to learn more about the room you're in, click on the 'Room Info' button. It's the small letter 'i' in the bottom left-hand corner of the game screen.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.navigation.navigator" CAPTION="Using the VMK Map">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[At the bottom of your screen you'll see a globe icon — this will give you an overview of the whole Kingdom. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[The Park Map shows all of the lands you'll recognize from the Parks; right at the center you'll see the Guest Rooms. Guest Rooms are the rooms created by other Players. Why don't you drop in to see what they're up to?]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[GAME SHORTCUTS\r
The Game Shortcuts will take you straight to VMK's games: Pirates of the Caribbean, Jungle Cruise Photo Safari, Street Party Music  Game and Castle Fireworks.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[LANDS\r
You can click on land names across the top of the map (such as Main Street and Fantasyland®), to zoom right into that area. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[ADVANCED MODE\r
Only select this mode if you're a true VMK pro and you want to navigate to a specific instance. All of the 'instances' of an area look the same but you'll find different people in each one.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Click on the name of a guest area to see a list of the available instances. Each instance has an indicator of how many guests are there. If one instance (e.g. 'South') is full, try another one.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[GUEST ROOMS\r
You can see the rooms of all of your online friends, and the rooms that are the most popular right now. The 'Own Rooms' tab will take you straight to your own room, where you can get busy furnishing, or host your own visitors.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.navigation.monorail" CAPTION="Monorail & Teleporters">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Once you've been in the Kingdom for a while, you'll learn that there are some more exclusive ways to get around. Find the secret Monorail stations to get around in style. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[ ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Or buy a set of Teleporters with a friend to get high-speed access to each other's rooms.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.navigation.following" CAPTION="Following a Friend">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If you want to explore VMK with a friend, you can just walk around together. But if you're trying to meet up and you're not sure where your friend is, go to the friend list in your 'Mail'.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Just click the envelope-shaped icon at the bottom of your game screen, and choose the 'Friends' tab. You'll see what room they're in and can then join them at the click of a button.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
 </HELPCATEGORY>
 <HELPCATEGORY CAPTION="Guest Rooms">
  <HELP NAME="help.rooms.buy" CAPTION="Buying a Room">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You get your very own piece of the Park, a Guest room that other VMK Players can visit. The first room comes free, and the more you hang out and play the games, the more credits you get to spend on furnishings and extra rooms!]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.rooms.furnish" CAPTION="Furnishing a Room">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Design Your Own Room
Create your very own room in the Kingdom when you join the game. The more you hang out and play, the more credits you get to spend on furnishings.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Once you've found the right place, you can rotate your furniture so that it fits just so. You can also move it somewhere else or click to 'Take Away'.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You only see these options around your furniture when you have the 'Furnishing Mode' on in your room. You can turn this mode on and off in the 'Room Info' window.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.rooms.change" CAPTION="Changing Room Info">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can change your room name and description at any time.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.rooms.teleporters" CAPTION="Teleporters">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Use Teleporters to move between Guest Rooms.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
 </HELPCATEGORY>
 <HELPCATEGORY CAPTION="Chat & Friends">
  <HELP NAME="help.messaging.chatting" CAPTION="Chat">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If you want to say something, type in the box at the bottom of the screen and hit the return key on your computer's keyboard.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[ALLOWED WORDS\r
To keep VMK safe and non-threatening, you can only chat using words that are in the VMK dictionary. Words that aren't considered suitable flash in red, and you'll have to change them before you can send your message to the room.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If you're having trouble saying what you want to (for example, if your favorite new song includes some words that aren't in our dictionary), you can suggest a new word to us via the CONTACT US form on the website: www.vmk.com]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[GETTING ATTENTION\r
As well as waving and dancing, you can throw emotes into your conversations and even trigger magic effects from chat. It will all come to you over time.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[MAGIC WORDS\r
You can also cast magic spells by typing a word in chat (if you own a magic pin). Just click on your pin to see what the magic word is!]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[IGNORE A PLAYER\r
If another player is annoying you, simply click on their character to open their profile, then select the red IGNORE button. You won't see another word they type!]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.messaging.filters" CAPTION="Allowed Words">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[To keep VMK safe and welcoming, you can only chat using words that are in VMK's allowed words list. Words that aren't recognized as suitable flash in red, and you'll have to change them before you can send your message to the room.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can't repeat a word or character - like ! or I - more than two times in a text field, either. The third time you type a word or character it will flash in red and you'll have to delete it.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[It is against the VMK way to use numbers in the game, especially to try to share personal information like your age or phone number. If VMK Staff find you trying to get around the allowed words list, you might be banned.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If you're having trouble saying what you want to (for example, if your favorite new song includes some words that aren't in our dictionary), you can suggest a new word to us via the Contact Us form on the website.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.chat.emotes" CAPTION="Emotes & Magic">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[EMOTES \r
Emotes are a quick way to express your feelings. You can choose an emote from the menu to the left of your chat bar, indicated by a heart-shaped icon. Simply double-click the Mickey face that suits your mood and it will show up in the room. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can also wave to your friends by clicking the 'Wave' button, or dance while you chat by clicking 'Dance'.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[MAGIC \r
You can only perform magic if you're wearing a magic pin. You choose the pins you want to wear from the Pins tab of your 'Stuff' menu, indicated by the chair-shaped icon at the bottom of the screen. Select your magic pin and then click 'Wear'.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[This magic effect will now be available from the magic menu to the right of your chat bar, indicated by a magic wand icon. Open the menu and double-click on your magic pin to impress your friends.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Click 'Stop' to end the effect. You have to wait for a while after using a magic effect to restore your powers.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[MAGIC WORDS \r
You can also cast magic spells by typing a word in chat (if you own a magic pin). Just click on your pin to see what the magic word is!]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[BlingBling! for Buried in Treasure \r
BoomCrash! for Cursed Storm \r
Inferno! for Dancing Inferno \r
Rocket! for Fireworks \r
Whoosh! for Flying Carpet \r
Spooky! for Ghost \r
YohoYoho! for Pirate Costume \r
Jump! for Teleportation \r]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.messaging.friends" CAPTION="Meeting People">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Seen someone interesting? Overheard an intriguing conversation? To get to know someone better, click on the Player's Character to view their profile. You'll see the name, signature and the Disney pins that Player is wearing.
]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can also see if they're someone special. There are 4 special status badges in VMK: \r
* VMK Staff\r
* Community Leader\r
* Born in Park\r
* VIP\r]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If they've got some interesting looking gear you might want to invite them to 'Trade'. And if you've been hanging out for a while and you're thinking you may want to catch up again, click on that Character and choose the 'Ask to be a Friend' button.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If they add you to their friends list, you can send messages and find each other in the Kingdom.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Finally, if you meet someone who's giving you grief, then you can ignore them. Click on their Character, choose the IGNORE button and you won't see another word they type.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.messaging.guide" CAPTION="Mail">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[VMK Mail lets you send messages to other players when they're offline, or in another area of VMK. You'll have to add a player to your 'Friends' list before you can send them messages. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You do this by clicking their Character and choosing the 'Ask to be a Friend' option on their profile. Once someone's on your friend list, you can send them messages or go to same room to chat.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Make sure you read and reply to your messages before you click 'Next' - otherwise they will be deleted before you get a chance to.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If you get a message that worries you, you can report it to VMK Staff and remove the sender from your friend list.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.messaging.control" CAPTION="Peace & Quiet">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If someone's hassling you, there are all sorts of things you can do to protect yourself. You can IGNORE them for a while, BOOT them from your guest room, or REPORT them to VMK Staff. And remember, you can always exit the game and come back later.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[IGNORE A PLAYER\r
Simply click on their character to open their profile. (Their profile is the window with their signature and pins.) Click the red IGNORE button and you won't see another word they type!]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[BOOT A PLAYER\r
If someone's causing trouble in your guest room you can boot them out. Open their profile, then click the red BOOT button. The troublesome player will be thrown out of your room and won't be allowed to return for 15 minutes.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[REPORT MESSAGES\r
If the person causing you trouble is on your list of friends, you can show their offensive messages to VMK Staff by clicking the red REPORT button. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[DELETE FRIEND\r
If you want to remove someone from your friend list, select their name and click the red DELETE button. This will stop them from sending you messages, and they won't be able to see your location in the game anymore.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[REPORT A PLAYER\r
If you're really worried about another player's behaviour, you can report them to VMK Staff.
Open their profile then click the red REPORT button. The CALL FOR HELP window will open with their guest name already filled in.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[CALL FOR HELP\r
To get emergency help at any time while you're playing the game, simply CALL FOR HELP by clicking the other tab in this window. A VMK staff member will then either send you a message or come and see you.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Talk to an adult you know well if you're worried or upset about anything that's happened online. If there is no adult you can speak to, or if you want to talk to someone in confidence, you can call Childhelp USA at 1-800-4-A-CHILD (1-800-422-4453).
]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.special.help" CAPTION="Call For Help">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[To get emergency help at any time while you're playing the game, simply 'Call For Help' by clicking the other tab in this window. A VMK staff member will then either send you a message or come and see you.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[The Call For Help option is VMK's 911 service, so please only use it in emergencies — if another Player is hassling you or making you feel uncomfortable. For general questions about the game, check this game guide.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
 </HELPCATEGORY>
 <HELPCATEGORY CAPTION="Credits & Stuff">
  <HELP NAME="help.stuff.credits" CAPTION="Credits">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Virtual Magic Kingdom is completely free to play, but that doesn't mean you get everything for nothing. You have to spend time in the Kingdom, exploring and playing the games to earn credits that you can then spend in the shops.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can earn credits by exploring the park, looking for Hidden Mickeys and characters like The Yeti and Shrunken Ned. You also get them for winning games and getting high scores, mixing your own music, or creating an award-winning Guest Room.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can see how much credit you have by viewing your stuff – click the chair-shaped icon at the bottom of the game screen and then select the 'Credit' tab. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[VMK credits never expire; you can let them pile up for as long as you like. But why would you when you could be decking out your very own pad in the Virtual Kingdom, instead?]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.stuff.codes" CAPTION="Codes">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[A secret code is a combination of letters and numbers that you can type into the game to receive either game credits or VMK virtual stuff. They are usually 16 characters and 3 hyphens. Here is an example: DUCK-8989-TINK-9870.
]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[How Do I Get One of These Codes? \r
* From the Disney Adventures magazine.\r
* On a special VMK trading card when you buy special merchandise at a Disney Theme Park\r
* By successfully completing a Quest at a Disney Theme Park]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Disney Adventures Magazine\r
Please note that the Disney Adventures magazine secret codes are only 14 characters long.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[How Do I Use One?\r
1. Open your 'Stuff' by clicking on the Chair icon.\r
2. Open the 'Codes' tab and type in your series of 16 letters and numbers.\r
3. You will receive a message when the item appears in your 'Stuff.']]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.stuff.shopping" CAPTION="Shopping">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[To collect more stuff, visit each shop to see what gear is in stock. You can get cool Disney-themed furnishings, loads of fashion items, collectible pins and posters. Collect pages for your Catalog by visiting all of the shops - every land has one!]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You'll need to return to the shops every now and again to see if they have any special offers. You can get to all of the shops easily by teleporting from the Emporium.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.stuff.refunds" CAPTION="Refunds">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Made an impulse buy? You can sell it back to us and use your credits for something else.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.stuff.trading" CAPTION="Trading">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[If you can't find what you want in the shops, you can try trading things with other Players. Just click on their Character and invite them to swap stuff with you.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[They will offer you some of the items they own and you can choose what you want to give them in exchange. Chat about it as you go. Nothing is final until you check the 'Accept' box. Remember to add them to your friend list if the trade goes well!]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Not every Player in the game is as honest as you might like them to be. Be sure the trade is complete before you click on Accept, or you may get ripped off.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.stuff.furniture" CAPTION="Furnishings">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can manage your Furnishings by viewing your 'Stuff' – click the Chair icon at the bottom of the screen and then select the Furnishings tab.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.stuff.clothes" CAPTION="Clothing">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can manage your Clothing by viewing your 'Stuff' – click the Chair icon at the bottom of the screen and then select the Clothing tab.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.stuff.pins" CAPTION="Pins">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can manage your Pins by viewing your 'Stuff' – click the Chair icon at the bottom of the screen and then select the Pins tab.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.stuff.posters" CAPTION="Posters">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can manage your Posters by viewing your 'Stuff' – click the Chair icon at the bottom of the screen and then select the Posters tab.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.stuff.rooms" CAPTION="Rooms">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can manage your Guest Rooms via the 'Map' – click the globe-shaped icon at the bottom of the screen and then select the Guest Rooms tab.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.stuff.camera" CAPTION="Camera">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Capture your adventures in VMK with a camera. You'll find the camera - plus film and a photo album for sharing your pictures - in VMK Central, on Main Street.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[VMK CENTRAL \r 
Click on the 'Dead Men Take No Pictures' poster to collect the right Catalog page. Your Catalog will open to the Camera Page. Buy the 'Camera and 3 film' product. (You'll need to make sure you have enough credits.)]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[TAKING PHOTOS \r 
Once you've bought the camera, simply click the camera icon at the bottom of your game screen to use it. Click 'Take Photo' in the Camera window, then line up your shot.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[The area of the screen that you photograph will be toned in sepia colors and can be saved to your Photo Catalog.\r
\r
Don't forget to add a caption, so you remember the moment!]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[PHOTO CATALOG \r 
The Photo Catalog includes all of the pictures you've taken and saved. Simply click the camera icon at the bottom of your game screen to open it. You can edit your captions, or choose a picture to place on the wall of your Guest Room. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[PHOTO ALBUM \r 
If you own a Photo Album, you can publish your best shots to it, and then set it up in one of your rooms for other players to view.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[CAMERA SUPPLIES \r 
When you run out of film, you can just buy more from the VMK Central page of your Shopping Catalog.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
 </HELPCATEGORY>
 <HELPCATEGORY CAPTION="Secret Codes">
  <HELP NAME="help.codes.kell" CAPTION="Kellogg's Pirate Powers">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[A secret code is a combination of letters and numbers that you can type into the game to receive either game credits or VMK virtual stuff.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can find special codes for magical Pirate Powers inside specially-marked packages of Kellogg's® Froot Loops®, Kellogg's® Apple Jacks®, Kellogg's® Rice Krispies®, & Kellogg's® Cinnamon Krunchers™ cereals.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[How Do I Use One?\r
1. Open your 'Stuff' by clicking on the Chair icon.\r
2. Open the 'Codes' tab and type in your series of 14 letters and numbers.\r
3. You will receive a message when the item appears in your 'Stuff.']]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can get 3 types of pirate magic: One where you become a swashbuckling pirate, another where you get swept away in a cursed storm and the last where you are buried in treasure!]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
 </HELPCATEGORY>
 <HELPCATEGORY CAPTION="Playing Games">
  <HELP NAME="help.games.pirates" CAPTION="Pirates of the Caribbean">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Two teams of up to four players each battle it out at sea. You'll captain your very own Pirate ship, unloading your cannons at your enemies and helping your team to victory. Fire at your enemies until their ships are sunk.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[CONTROLS \r Left Mouse Button Click - Your ship will sail towards where you click \r Left Mouse Button Double-Click - Fires cannons on the side of the ship that you click \r Left & Right Arrow Key - Double press to fire to that side of your ship.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[STARTING THE GAME \r The POTC Game Lobby is where the battles begin. You can join a game that someone else is starting, or start a new game of your own. The games, teams, and team members are shown in the lower part of the screen.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Use the arrow buttons on the sides of the games list to browse through the games that are about to start. You can play Level 2 and Level 3 games after you've won enough games at the previous level.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[HOW TO NAVIGATE \r Your ship is indicated by an arrow. Click the map on the spot you want to get to and your ship will start sailing towards it. A blue wheel marks the spot you clicked on. Make sure there's open water between you and your destination.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[HOW TO SHOOT \r Double press the left or right arrow keys on your keyboard - or double-click with your mouse on the map - to shoot. The ship will fire a volley of cannonballs from the side you choose (left or right).]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Your ship has limited ammo so make sure you take aim before you fire! Press the arrow key once to check where your cannons are aimed. Your health is shown as first-aid crates at the bottom of the screen. If you run out of health, your ship is sunk.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[STAYING IN THE GAME \r You can pick up more ammo and health by sailing over the floating cannonballs and crates in the sea. After you've taken your final hit, you can explode your gunpowder reserves by double-clicking your shipwreck.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.games.jungle" CAPTION="Jungle Cruise Photo Safari">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Skipper your boat through a remote forest, looking for new critters, as they pop in and out of view. Be quick with your camera to get the 'perfect shot' before they disappear. And keep an eye on your Gas - your cruise is over as soon as you run out.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[CONTROLS\r
Left Arrow Key - Move left \r
Right Arrow Key - Move right \r 
Up Arrow Key – Speed\r
Down Arrow Key - Slow down\r 
Mouse - Move camera target\r
Left Mouse Button - Take photo]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[HOW TO PHOTOGRAPH\r
Move your camera target over a Critter until it's centered in the shot and your target turns red. Then click your mouse button to take a photo - the better your aim, the more points you get!
]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[STAYING IN THE GAME\r
You can see a counter of how much Film and Gas you have left in the top right of the screen. You can collect Film and Gas top-ups by running over the Film Canisters and Gas Tanks in the river.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[HAZARDS \r
Be a careful skipper! Keep away from the river's shore and rocks, and make sure you snap any Critters that get in your way. If your boat hits something it shouldn't, it'll be damaged and you'll lose valuable Gas.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[It's all over when you run out of Gas, and you'll be returned to the Dock. Once there, you'll see a scrapbook of the Critters you photographed, and your final score. Play again and try to get to the high score list - the best Skippers get lots of credit!]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.games.fireworks" CAPTION="Castle Fireworks">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Compete against 100 other people to create the most explosive pyrotechnics show!]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[STARTING THE GAME \r 
The countdown will start when the first guest clicks 'Play', and the show will begin as soon as there are 100 players. (If there are at least 10 of you - and you've been waiting for 5 minutes - the game will start anyway.)]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[CONTROLS \r Mouse - Control fireworks target \r Left Mouse Button - Explode the targeted firework \r Left Arrow Key - Move fireworks icon selector to the left \r Right Arrow Key - Move the fireworks icon selector to the right]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[HOW TO PLAY \r Check out the fireworks as they're launched from the ground and arm your cursor by selecting a matching icon from the bottom of the screen. Your cursor will be transformed into the icon you select.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Explode the firework by clicking it with your matching cursor. The firework blinks faster and faster as it gets closer to the highest point of its path through the sky. Explode it at the very top for the most spectacular display and highest points.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[LEVELS \r There are 5 levels, each with a different view of the Kingdom and new Disney music. There are also 3 rounds per level and they get more and more challenging because the number of firework icons to choose from increases. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[PROGRESS \r Only the best players from each level progress to the next, and only a select few will get to see the final, spectacular view of the whole Park. Between each level you'll see the highest scores, and your position in the rankings.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.games.music" CAPTION="Street Party Music">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You are the mix master, so build, play and save your own music with this awesome music mixing tool. Host a party on Main Street and watch everyone move to your grooves.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[CONTROLS \r
Mouse – Control sample selection\r 
Left Mouse Button Single Click – Places the selected sample on a track\r
Left Mouse Button Double Click – Removes the selected sample from a track]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[STARTING THE GAME\r
Enter the Street Party Music Game from the Street Party Music Game Lobby, or from your Map. You will be given the option to ‘Create’ a new mix.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[HOW TO MIX\r
Check out the samples by moving your mouse cursor over them. You'll hear each sample when you hover above it. Click on a sound to choose it, then click on the track on the slot where you want to place the instrument.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can remove a sample from a track by double-clicking on it. Press 'Play' at any time to hear your mix and 'Clear all' if you want to start again. Once you’re happy with your music, give it a name and 'Save' it.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[HOW TO PLAY\r
Return to the Street Party Music Game Lobby and walk your Character to the decks on the stage. You'll join a queue and be asked to choose your mix. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Select a song and you will be automatically advanced to the decks, where you'll play your tune for everyone and dance along with your virtual friends.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.games.scores" CAPTION="High Scores">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[The more games you win, or get high scores in, the more credits you earn to spend in VMK. You also get to show off in the top-score tables on the VMK Web site.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.games.own" CAPTION="Guest Room Gaming">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Become a Game Designer!
Some of the most popular Guest rooms in VMK are gaming rooms, where the owners give away their own VMK goodies to the Players who win their races or quizzes.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can create games using nothing more than furnishings, the room description and your own wild imagination. Check out the Tools of the Ride Operators in the Emporium page of the Shopping Catalog and start planning.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[  
]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
 </HELPCATEGORY>
 <HELPCATEGORY CAPTION="Exploring the Kingdom">
  <HELP NAME="help.explore.mickey" CAPTION="Hidden Mickey Quest">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[FIND HIDDEN MICKEY\r
A Hidden Mickey is a silhouette of Mickey Mouse's head and ears, concealed somewhere in the scenery. Take a photo with your in-game camera and you'll be on your way to winning exclusive VMK loot.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You'll find the camera in VMK Central, on Main Street. That's also where you should return to check on how many Mickeys you've found.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.explore.npc" CAPTION="Finding Disney Characters">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Get the most out of VMK when you explore the Guest areas. You can win exclusive pins in the game by finding Disney Characters like The Yeti and Munificent, the Dragon.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.explore.photos" CAPTION="Taking Photos">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Capture your adventures in VMK with a camera. You'll find the camera - plus film and a photo album for sharing your pictures - in VMK Central.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.explore.shops" CAPTION="Visiting Shops">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[To collect more stuff, visit each shop to see what gear is in stock. You won't see a shop's catalog page until you've visited it at least once.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You'll need to return every now and again to see if it has any special offers. You can get to all of the shops easily by teleporting from the Emporium.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.explore.monorail" CAPTION="Finding the Monorail">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Once you've been in the Kingdom for a while, you'll learn that there are some more exclusive ways to get around. Find the hidden Monorail stations to get around in style. Board the rail and venture to your favorite areas at high speed. ]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.about.magic" CAPTION="Sampling Magic">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Just a select few players will acquire magical spells to give them extra powers while playing VMK. Each spell gives them a unique chance to show off their ability while in the VMK world.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[There are four magic spells in effect in the Kingdom: Teleportation Magic, Dancing Inferno Magic, Invisibility Magic and Fireworks Magic. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Acquire one and you may soon find yourself burning up the stage in the Street Party Music Game lobby or casually teleporting around the place. ]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
 </HELPCATEGORY>
 <HELPCATEGORY CAPTION="Music & Sound">
  <HELP NAME="help.music.prefs" CAPTION="Sound Preferences">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[To change VMK's sound settings, open your 'Preferences' menu by clicking the t-shirt icon at the bottom of the game screen. Select the 'Sound' tab.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[There are 3 types of sound in VMK: Music, Sound Effects and Game Interface. Check the box next to a sound type to turn that sound on; uncheck the box to turn sound off.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can also change the volume of all sound using the slider - drag it closer to 'Loud' to increase the sound, and down to 'Silent' to mute it.\r
\r
Click 'OK' when you're done.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.music.mix" CAPTION="Mixing Your Own Music">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Create your own music mix and get the whole world dancing along! Enter the Street Party Music Game from the Street Party Music Game Lobby, or from your Map. You will be given the option to 'Create' a new mix.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[CONTROLS \r
Mouse – Control sample selection\r 
Left Mouse Button Single Click – Places the selected sample on a track\r
Left Mouse Button Double Click – Removes the selected sample from a track\r]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[HOW TO MIX\r
Check out the samples by moving your mouse cursor over them. You'll hear each sample when you hover above it. Click on a sound to choose it, then click on the track on the slot where you want to place the instrument.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You can remove a sample from a track by double-clicking on it. Press 'Play' at any time to hear your mix and 'Clear all' if you want to start again. Once you're happy with your music, give it a name and 'Save' it.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
  <HELP NAME="help.music.play" CAPTION="Playing Your Own Music">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[You are the mix master, so build, play and save your own music. Enter the Street Party Music Game from the Street Party Music Game Lobby, and 'Create' a new mix.

]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[HOW TO PLAY \r
Return to the Street Party Music Game Lobby and walk your Character to the decks on the stage. You'll join a queue and be asked to choose your mix. ]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[Select a song and you will be automatically advanced to the decks, where you'll play your tune for everyone and dance along with your virtual friends.]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
 </HELPCATEGORY>
 <HELPCATEGORY CAPTION="In-Park Quests">
  <HELP NAME="help.quests.central" CAPTION="VMK Central">
   <PAGE><![CDATA[VMK Central is the place to go to find out everything there is to know about Disney's Virtual Magic Kingdom. Take off on a Hidden Mickey Quest, find out how to take a real Disney theme park quest, and discover how to take photos in VMK!]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[In-Park Quests start in July 2005! A VMK Quest is a challenge that takes place in a real Disney Theme Park. You must follow clues to discover secrets that will 'Unleash the Magic' of VMK by giving secret codes to exclusive powers and prizes.]]></PAGE>
   <PAGE><![CDATA[
]]></PAGE>
  </HELP>
